  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Thursday...\n\nTroughing and a surface low over southeast MT is expected to\ncontinue to bring scattered to widespread showers and some\nembedded thunderstorms through the overnight hours, gradually\nclearing through the morning. Another weak disturbance is \nexpected to move through under southwest flow aloft this afternoon\nand evening. Modest CAPE values generally less than 1000 J/kg and\nbulk shear at 20-30 kts may bring a few strong thunderstorms, but\ncloud cover may limit the instability. With precipitable water \nvalues remaining elevated through the next couple days, the main \nthreat with any storm will continue to be heavy rain. Another wave\nis expected to move through Saturday afternoon and evening with \ndryer air moving in behind. Moderate to high chances for at least \na half an inch of precipitation through Saturday remains across a \nmajority of the region, excluding southeast MT where a low chance \nexists. Chances for at least an inch of precipitation for this \nsame time period looks best for areas west of Billings (50-80%).\nContinue to use caution if recreating near any burn scars over the\nnext couple days. \n\nAlthough slightly drier air moves in and mid level heights return\nto near normal, the region maintains a slight southwesterly flow\naloft with southeasterly flow in the lower levels. Although no\nprominent disturbances are showing in the ensembles, this pattern\nwill give way to continued daily low to moderate chances for \nafternoon showers and thunderstorms next week. \n\nHigh temperatures will be in the uppers 60s and 70s today and\nSaturday, warming into the 70s and 80s for next week. TS",
